.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_BODY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_body \- access the buffered request body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const void *chttpsvr_req_body(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                               size_t *len_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a pointer to the buffered bytes of the request body and, when
len_out is not NULL, stores the body length in bytes in len_out.  It
returns NULL and stores 0 when the request has no body, and also when
req belongs to a streaming route registered with
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler: the server never reads the body
of a streaming route in advance, so use chttpsvr_req_read for such a
route instead.

The buffer stays valid for the duration of the handler call.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
